<title>FINLAND: MERITA TO CO-FINANCE INDONESIA PULP MILL.</title>
<headline>MERITA TO CO-FINANCE INDONESIA PULP MILL.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish bank group Merita Oy said on Thursday it is among the financiers of an Indonesian pulp mill project worth $1.3 billion in total.</p>
<p>&quot;Merita will be Intercreditor Agent for all of the lenders,&quot; Merita said in a statement.</p>
<p>Other Finnish parties involved in the project were Finnish Export Credit, engineering group Rauma Oy's Sunds Defibrator unit, privately-owned engineering and specialty paper group A.Ahlstrom Oy and forest industry consulting company Jaakko Poyry, part of the Finvest Oy group. -- Helsinki newsroom +358-9-6805 0248, news@Reuters.fi</p>
</text>
